From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:37:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: apple-dart: admit the J604 external display DARTs

The J604 (MacBook Pro 14-inch, M4) has the same two external display
pipes as the J713: dcpext0/1 with their firmware DARTs (dart-dcpext0/1,
SID23) and display DARTs (dart-dispext0/1, SID0/SID16) at the same
addresses. Its device tree lists those DART nodes with the same
registers, interrupts, tunables, mapper streams and segment names as the
J713's (25G83 templates; only phandle references differ).

Admit the J604 to the J713 external display DART adoption through a
board table, as the internal retained display already is. Nothing else
changes: a DART is adopted only when the boot loader marked its dcpext
apple,t8132-dcpext-firmware-ready = <1>, and without that marker the
probe leaves the inherited DART untouched, as on the J713. The J604
device tree does not describe these DARTs yet, so on its own this
change is inert on the J604.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index e98891b0db..3cded361f9 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -4105,6 +4105,25 @@ static bool apple_dart_display_admitted_at_boot(void)
 	return of_machine_compatible_match(apple_dart_display_boot_admit_boards);
 }
 
+/*
+ * T8132 boards whose loader may hand the external display coprocessors
+ * (dcpext0/1) over running. Their firmware and display DARTs are the same
+ * SoC blocks at the same addresses on both boards (dart-dcpext0/1 and
+ * dart-dispext0/1 in the J604 and J713 device trees). Being listed here
+ * admits nothing by itself: a DART is adopted only once the loader marked
+ * its dcpext apple,t8132-dcpext-firmware-ready.
+ */
+static const char *const apple_dart_dcpext_boards[] = {
+	"apple,j713",
+	"apple,j604",
+	NULL
+};
+
+static bool apple_dart_dcpext_board(void)
+{
+	return of_machine_compatible_match(apple_dart_dcpext_boards);
+}
+
 /*
  * Boards whose loader leaves the MTP (keyboard and trackpad) coprocessor
  * running with every stream of its T8110 DART at 0x394800000 in bypass.
@@ -4139,11 +4158,11 @@ static int apple_dart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t8132-dart") &&
 		(res->start == 0x30a300000ULL || res->start == 0x30a340000ULL);
 	/* The external DCP firmware DARTs (SID23) of dcpext0 and dcpext1. */
-	j713_dcpext = res && !tunneled && of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713") &&
+	j713_dcpext = res && !tunneled && apple_dart_dcpext_board() &&
 		of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t8132-dart") &&
 		(res->start == 0x286340000ULL || res->start == 0x48a340000ULL);
 	/* The external display DARTs (SID0/SID16) of dispext0 and dispext1. */
-	j713_dispext = res && !tunneled && of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713") &&
+	j713_dispext = res && !tunneled && apple_dart_dcpext_board() &&
 		of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t8132-dart") &&
 		(res->start == 0x286300000ULL || res->start == 0x48a300000ULL);
 	/* The J713 radio DART's fault interrupt is not described by its loader. */
